<title>USA: National Instruments says CFO resigns.</title>
<headline>National Instruments says CFO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Instruments said on Thursday that Joel Rollins, its vice president of finance and chief financial officer, had resigned to pursue interests in a startup company.</p>
<p>Rollins, who leaves the company in June, will be succeeded as chief financial officer by Alex Davern, currently serving as corporate controller, National Instruments said.</p>
<p>National Instruments manufactures software and hardware products for PCs and workstations.</p>
